+# Cancelling a Booked Visit Stays Out of Scope
+
+**Status:** Accepted. Narrows NG-5 in [Deleting Records and Amending Booked Visits Are Deliberately Out of Scope](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md).
+
+## Context
+
+NG-5 was confirmed deliberate on 2026-08-08 as one row covering two capabilities: changing a booked visit and cancelling one. That ADR set the terms for reopening either — an explicit owner decision recorded at intake, with its own non-goal ADR.
+
+A visit could be booked but never corrected, so a wrong date or a wrong description stayed wrong. The owner raised the gap on 2026-09-07 and decided the row.
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-5 whole.** Rejected by the owner: a record the clinic cannot correct is a gap the sample teaches nothing by keeping.
+2. **Open NG-5 entirely.** Rejected: cancellation carries lifecycle state — a visit that exists but no longer counts — which the sample models nowhere.
+3. **Narrow NG-5 to cancellation alone** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+The owner's decision, quoted from the intake record:
+
+> Non-goal NG-5 is narrowed: cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope, but correcting its date and description is now in.
+
+Correcting a booked visit's date and description becomes REQ-VIS-003. Cancelling one remains out of scope, and NG-5 now names cancellation alone. The sample still corrects records forward and still removes nothing: NG-4 is untouched, so deleting a visit stays out.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The forward-only correction pattern now covers owners, pets, and visits alike.
+- No visit carries a cancelled or void state, so the owner's record continues to list every visit a pet has.
+- Reopening the cancellation half needs a fresh owner decision recorded at intake, on the same terms the 2026-08-08 ADR set.
+- The correction form has no visible entry point in this decision. A route to it from the owner's record is open work, recorded as an open question in the PRD.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-5
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [REQ-VIS-003](../prd.md#req-vis-003) — the capability the narrowing opens.
